4-602.13:  Observed the following non-food contact surfaces to be soiled:
1) tracks and fans of the sliding glass door in kitchen (food crumbs and spills);
2) lowboys in the kitchen (food crumbs and debris);
3) fryers (grease accumulation);
4) around soda guns and triple sink of the outside bar space (syrup splash).
Clean these aforementioned areas. 

NonFOOD-CONTACT SURFACES of EQUIPMENT shall be cleaned at a frequency necessary to preclude accumulation of soil residues.

6-501.11: Observed the following areas to need repairs/cleaning:
1) Mold located near the back triple sink (look around the soiled side of the dish board); 
2) Tile cracked near floor drain by the back dish machine;
3) Floor air vents behind the bar observed to be dusty;
4) leak on the floor by the sliding door salad preparation cooler/air conditioner in kitchen (coming from drain line?). See that drain line isn’t leaking onto floor.


Discussed cleaning and maintenancewith PIC. Ensure facility is cleaned at a frequency to prevent mold/dust accumulation. 
6-501.11: PHYSICAL FACILITIES shall be maintained in good repair.
